  <title>Voice sets</title>
  <p>
    A voice set contains four voice types: default, uppercase, hyperlink, and system. You can
    configure these voice types for the Global voice set, which normally applies. You can also
    create additional voice sets for the languages you frequently use and configure the
    language, person, rate, pitch, inflection, and volume for each voice type in those voice
    sets.
  </p>
  <p>
    The default voice reads ordinary text. The uppercase voice identifies capital letters, the
    hyperlink voice identifies links, and the system voice presents information supplied by
    Orca, such as object roles. These voice choices are separate from Global Voice Settings,
    which controls behavior shared by all voice types.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each configured voice set also has an unbound command for switching directly to that voice
    set. The voice parameter commands temporarily adjust the active voice set. To save changes
    or configure individual voice types, use the settings below.
  </p>
